$openpose — OpenPose skeleton maps from images

SUMMARY
  Detects human pose keypoints and renders a classic OpenPose stick-figure map
  (colored limbs on a black background) for each input image.

SYNTAX
  $openpose
  $openpose(detect_resolution=512, hand=0, face=0)

INPUT
  images[] — source photos or frames.

OUTPUT
  images[] — skeleton map PNGs (same count as input).

ARGUMENTS
  detect_resolution=512 — resize long side for detection (higher = finer detail).
  hand=0 — set to 1 to include hand keypoints (needs hand_pose_model.pth).
  face=0 — set to 1 to include face landmarks (needs facenet.pth).

SETUP
  models/openpose/ (body_pose_model.pth; optional hand/face weights).
  Download:
    uv run python tools/download_models.py --upstream-fallback
  .venvs/media with controlnet-aux + torch. GPU when CUDA is available.
  AH_OPENPOSE_GPU=0 forces CPU inference.

EXAMPLE
  @pose_maps: $folder('refs') -> $openpose(detect_resolution=768)
  @control: $file('model.png') -> $openpose(hand=1, face=1) -> $image2image(...)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
